    "raw_public_english_response": "The read-only Registry V2 stress assessment for case `gaussian-raw-route-functional-invalid` is complete and the plan was accepted.\n\n**Evidence consulted (read-only):**\n- `expected.functional` V1 view: inventory available, but **0 matched values and no rule IDs** — no frozen functional receipt discharges this case; assessment falls to deterministic project semantics.\n- `expected.basis` V1 view: inventory available with `def2-SVP` listed (along with `def2-SV(P)` etc.) — advisory only; a discoverable name is not automatically native/compiler-ready.\n\n**Assessment:**\n- The typed functional `B3LYP nosymm` embeds the native route keyword `nosymm` (a symmetry route flag) inside the functional field. Route content is not part of a functional specification, so the literal is an **invalid specification** → readiness `blocked_invalid_specification`.\n- Source literals preserved: functional `B3LYP nosymm`, basis `def2-SVP`.\n- No elements were specified in the request, so no element/ECP findings were asserted.\n- No native input, command, project write, or execution: all four guarded fields are `false`.\n\n**Submission receipt (case-bound normalization, V1.0.0):**\n- Raw contract valid; no conflicting explicit settings; the normalizer deterministically filled `settings.freq = true` to match the `freq` task kind.\n- Receipt SHA-256: `f5f38a43e82f002fef405d37f633e504ee9b6cb1fcc5a207471a5f30f6e1ccb3`\n\nThe proposal stands blocked on the malformed functional; no execution or project writes were performed.",
